# =============================================================================
#  ISPFlow - FreeRADIUS accounting policy (Acct-Start / Interim / Stop).
#
#  INLINED into the site's `accounting { }` section by install-vps.sh, for the
#  same reason as authorize: FreeRADIUS 3.2.5 rejects a top-level `if` in a
#  module file, a policy.d file or an $INCLUDEd file.
#
#  Accounting keeps post-auth honest. post-auth opens the session when the login
#  succeeds; these packets carry the byte counters, the running time and the
#  termination reason, and they are what the bill is built from.
#
#  Tenant safety: the statements are keyed on acct_session_id AND nas_identifier,
#  and isp_id is taken from radius_nas. A router cannot write accounting against
#  another router's session even if it guesses the session id.
#
#  Deliberately NOT done here:
#
#    * Deactivation. Writing an acct_stop on shutdown would cut every live
#      customer whenever FreeRADIUS restarted or lost its database. Sessions are
#      closed by the router's Acct-Stop and by the worker for a deliberate
#      disconnect. A RADIUS restart must not be an outage.
#
#  ------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Why this section contains no `if`
#  ------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The accounting section does not accept one:
#
#      sites-enabled/default[873]: Invalid location for 'if'
#
#  Unlike authorize and post-auth, `accounting { }` is not a full unlang section
#  in FreeRADIUS 3.2.5, so a conditional here is a startup failure, not a
#  runtime one. Any decision that would have been made by a conditional has to be
#  made in SQL instead, which is where it belongs anyway: the statements use
#  NULLIF and COALESCE so an absent attribute degrades to the last known value.
# =============================================================================

# Invoking the module IS the call: in the accounting section rlm_sql picks the
# statement for this packet's Acct-Status-Type out of the `accounting { }` block
# in queries.conf and runs it. There is no sql_query() function in FreeRADIUS 3.
#
# An accounting failure must never reject or drop the request. The router has
# already billed itself; failing the packet would lose the session record. A
# later Interim-Update repairs anything missed.
sql